<article class="env-definition" id="065W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065W">Definition <span data-tag="065W">22.3.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \text{d})$, $(B, \text{d})$ be differential graded algebras over $R$. The <em>tensor product differential graded algebra</em> of $A$ and $B$ is the algebra $A \otimes _ R B$ with multiplication defined by </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (a \otimes b)(a' \otimes b') = (-1)^{\deg (a')\deg (b)} aa' \otimes bb'  \]
</div>
  <p> endowed with differential $\text{d}$ defined by the rule $\text{d}(a \otimes b) = \text{d}(a) \otimes b + (-1)^ m a \otimes \text{d}(b)$ where $m = \deg (a)$. </p>
</article>